each whose body copies a field of the element into a list whose elements do
not accept every value of it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: close({
	u!: [...close({id!: int})]
})
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: close({
	u!: [...string]
})

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		u: _each(v0_0.u, _item.id)
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: close({u!: [...string]})
-- out/error --
error[E0359]: the ForwardLens in history/1.0.thema copies u[].id into the elements of u, which do not accept every value of it
 --> history/1.0.thema:8:20
  |
8 |         u: _each(v0_0.u, _item.id)
  |                          ^^^^^
  |
  = note: u[] in 1.0 was int and is now string (copying _item.id; compatibility rule value-narrowed)
  = help: copy into u a field whose values its elements accept, or map them with a struct of mappings
